{"id": "EUVD-2026-81860", "enisaUuid": "751a42e3-663f-3c67-9415-8f9566af6e0f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nscsi: sd: Fix special_vec mempool leak when scsi_alloc_sgtables() fails\n\nsd_set_special_bvec() allocates a special payload page for UNMAP and\nWRITE SAME commands. If scsi_alloc_sgtables() fails afterward in\nsd_setup_unmap_cmnd() or sd_setup_write_same{10,16}_cmnd(), the SCSI\nmidlayer does not call uninit_command() because RQF_DONTPREP is not set\nyet, leaking the page.\n\nCall sd_uninit_command() on error, and clear RQF_SPECIAL_PAYLOAD after\nfreeing the page.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:08:02", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:50:46", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/710a2448a06a8215ba8acb4a2791954800f7db0a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/744a65e113094756e6c1cfba9ff1bf4247cb68d4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e90f746f4ca3896ca560e820b7b6b0a467026938", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5d7d1b8b525e5eff33a01d07dfcf7bdd3b6d790d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bb31844d88b77138b67aa20c3600203baff40140"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90267", "GHSA-pf2c-jgx6-jjwq"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "37a2547d-2c11-3fab-9716-2e0d13176120", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "4cdee431-7055-3934-a561-186df271b5bf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "81d926e8b5520e38f1f72dd7bb7cfc81c1a69d87 <744a65e113094756e6c1cfba9ff1bf4247cb68d4"}, {"id": "518c82f3-3dae-330b-a073-5f5806bc692f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "53f83cd5-e282-30d8-9e17-0e3bd93dfb36", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "a0f2227a-79f3-3334-80ae-946a135b9eb4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_versio